# Extra packages to remove, beyond Omarchy's preinstalls (which the remove
# module handles through `omarchy-remove-preinstalls`). One per line.
#
# omarchy-pkg-drop runs `pacman -Rns`, which refuses to break dependencies, so
# a package something else needs survives the sweep. When a removal is
# refused, `pacman -Qi <pkg>` names what still requires it.

# Displaced by the defaults in overlay.conf: Emacs is the editor, Ghostty the
# terminal, Firefox Developer Edition the browser.
omarchy-nvim
neovim
foot
chromium
